        sourceType = "Achievement",
        difficulty = "easy",
        difficultyReason = "Travel to seventeen critters and use an emote.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Easy - Travel to seventeen critters and use an emote.\n\n1. Track the seventeen named critters. This is an EMOTE achievement: target a living outdoor critter and type /love. Capturing the pet, summoning your own companion or killing it is unnecessary. Turn on nameplates/target by exact name; not every eligible critter appears under Track Pets.\n\n2. Find a living Leopard Tree Frog around 51,55 on the selected map and use /love while targeting it. These are reported search areas for wandering critters, not guaranteed stationary spawns.\n\n3. Find a living Shrine Fly around 36,58 on the selected map and use /love while targeting it. These are reported search areas for wandering critters, not guaranteed stationary spawns.\n\n4. Find a living Coral Adder around 64,82 on the selected map and use /love while targeting it. These are reported search areas for wandering critters, not guaranteed stationary spawns.\n\n5. Find a living Dancing Water Skimmer around 32,68 on the selected map and use /love while targeting it. These are reported search areas for wandering critters, not guaranteed stationary spawns. Use Zidormi's earlier Pandaria Vale if the assault phase changes the local wildlife.\n\n6. Find a living Gilded Moth around 69,38 on the selected map and use /love while targeting it. These are reported search areas for wandering critters, not guaranteed stationary spawns. Use Zidormi's earlier Pandaria Vale if the assault phase changes the local wildlife.\n\n7. Find a living Golden Civet around 69,26 on the selected map and use /love while targeting it. These are reported search areas for wandering critters, not guaranteed stationary spawns. Use Zidormi's earlier Pandaria Vale if the assault phase changes the local wildlife.\n\n8. Find a living Sifang Otter around 64,65 on the selected map and use /love while targeting it. These are reported search areas for wandering critters, not guaranteed stationary spawns.\n\n9. Find a living Band