    [6537] = {
        achievementId = 6537,
        name = "Slum It in the Summit",
        source = "Slum It in the Summit",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        difficulty = "medium",
        difficultyReason = "Several connected story chapters with separate local branches.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Several connected story chapters with separate local branches.\n\n1. Enable Trivial Quests and use an Alliance character. The quest panel below selects this character's next incomplete quest; account achievement credit does not necessarily mean a fresh character has completed its prerequisites.\n\n2. Westwind Rest: Start in Binan Village with the arrows, injured-warrior and yaungol-leader errands. Speak to the awakened faction commander, travel to your faction's rest and finish Challenge Accepted. The three awakened-commander handoffs are equivalent versions, not three mandatory repeats.\n\n3. Inkgill Mere: At Binan/Inkgill accept Enraged Vengeance, Free the Dissenters and The Waterspeaker's Staff. Finish all three, perform The Ritual, cleanse the mere and defeat Shai Hu. This independent local branch does not require completing the entire northern story first.\n\n4. The Burlap Trail: At One Keg escort The Burlap Trail caravan to Burlap Waystation. Rescue Rabbitsfoot, recover his luckydo and finish the Monkey Idol, packs and Broketooth branches. Free the grummles, release the yeti and kill The Leader Hozen. Wait for escort arrival credit before leaving.\n\n5. The Thunder King: Follow Cho's missive and One Keg's mountain-supply quests into the Valley of Emperors. Complete Seeker's Folly, It Was Almost Alive, Tomb of Shadows and Breaking the Emperor's Shield, then Stealing Their Thunder King.\n\n6. Zouchin Village: Continue from the tomb through Lessons from History and Chasing the Storm, then Fisherman's Tale. At Zouchin complete the training, weapons, village and supplies errands, defend the village in Enemies At Our Door and finish Revelations.\n\n7. The Yaungol Invasion: From the faction rest, finish its food, farmstead and mogu branches before the invasion tasks. Use the explosive barrels, free prisoners and stop the tent channelers, then defeat the Ordo Warbringer. Use your faction's quest variants; the duplicate final quest IDs represent alternate handoffs.\n\n8. The Yak Wash: Travel to Muskpaw Ranch, find the missing Muskpaw, wash the yaks and complete Yakity Yak, then Back in Yak. The Horde/Alliance ranch breadcrumbs are alternatives.\n\n9. Kota Peak: Find Kota Blend at Kota Basecamp, collect the brew ingredients and complete A Fair Trade. Use the supplied yeti transformation to smash attackers for The Burlap Grind; ordinary character kills do not replace the vehicle's objective.\n\n10. Temple of the White Tiger: Take your faction's Temple of the White Tiger quest, meet the temple's party and complete A Celestial Experience's trials. Finish its hand-in. This is the story visit, not the rotating August Celestials daily tournament.\n\n11. The Shado-Pan: From Binan finish the fallback defense and rage-trap quest, go to Winter's Blossom, honor the fallen and take the kite to the Ox Gate. Complete both wall-defense branches and the rolling-barrel encounter, then Where Are My Reinforcements? and Unbelievable! Stay for the scripted events.\n\n12. Finish each chapter's final hand-in and check its named criterion. The route keeps parallel errands and faction alternatives separate. If the current NPC is in a story phase, finish the active quest or use the campaign transport; flying to a later-phase map pin does not complete a vehicle, escort or vision objective.",
        stepCount = 12,
        waypoints = {
            { mapID = 379, x = 0.722, y = 0.9179999999999999, step = 1, label = "Binan Village - story start" },
            { mapID = 379, x = 0.58, y = 0.614, step = 1, label = "One Keg - Burlap caravan" },
            { mapID = 379, x = 0.6859999999999999, y = 0.431, step = 1, label = "White Tiger Temple" },
        },
        sources = { "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=6537#comments" },
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=6537",
        sourceURL = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=6537#comments",
        reviewedAt = "2026-11-13",
    },
    [6538] = {
