est IDs represent alternate handoffs.\n\n8. The Yak Wash: Travel to Muskpaw Ranch, find the missing Muskpaw, wash the yaks and complete Yakity Yak, then Back in Yak. The Horde/Alliance ranch breadcrumbs are alternatives.\n\n9. Kota Peak: Find Kota Blend at Kota Basecamp, collect the brew ingredients and complete A Fair Trade. Use the supplied yeti transformation to smash attackers for The Burlap Grind; ordinary character kills do not replace the vehicle's objective.\n\n10. Temple of the White Tiger: Take your faction's Temple of the White Tiger quest, meet the temple's party and complete A Celestial Experience's trials. Finish its hand-in. This is the story visit, not the rotating August Celestials daily tournament.\n\n11. The Shado-Pan: From Binan finish the fallback defense and rage-trap quest, go to Winter's Blossom, honor the fallen and take the kite to the Ox Gate. Complete both wall-defense branches and the rolling-barrel encounter, then Where Are My Reinforcements? and Unbelievable! Stay for the scripted events.\n\n12. Finish each chapter's final hand-in and check its named criterion. The route keeps parallel errands and faction alternatives separate. If the current NPC is in a story phase, finish the active quest or use the campaign transport; flying to a later-phase map pin does not complete a vehicle, escort or vision objective.",
