        },
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=7381",
        sourceURL = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=7381#comments",
        reviewedAt = "2026-11-13",
    },
    [7385] = {
        achievementId = 7385,
        name = "Pub Crawl",
        source = "Pub Crawl",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        difficulty = "hard",
        difficultyReason = "Eleven brewing-scenario challenges include random defenses and protected objectives.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Eleven brewing-scenario challenges include random defenses and protected objectives.\n\n1. Use Lorewalker Fu at Vale 83.2,30.6 to enter the four brewing scenarios. Track the eleven named criteria and use their individual numbered guides; their maps and tactics distinguish protection, speed and random-spawn attempts.\n\n2. In Unga Ingoo complete Spill No Evil, The Keg Runner, Monkey in the Middle and Monkey See, Monkey Kill. Do the no-theft and speed objectives on separate solo attempts; repeat optional boss checks until all seven named targets are credited.\n\n3. In Brewmoon Festival personally use all six random defenses for Binan Village All-Star, then prevent every building fire for Yaungolian Barbecue. Intercept Qobi outside the village and face his fire away from buildings.\n\n4. In A Brewing Storm complete Don't Shake the Keg, The Perfect Pour and Party of Six: avoid Swamp Smash and lightning, and preserve all six guardians. In Greenstone Village complete Perfect Delivery and Save it for Later: six undamaged kegs and no use of Volatile Greenstone Brew.\n\n5. Check all eleven criteria and learn the awarded Honorary Brewmaster Keg. The current tooltip specifies account-wide progress; historical single-character warnings predate that change. If an earned keg was destroyed before learning it, ask The Metal Paw in Binan Village about a replacement.",
        stepCount = 5,
        waypoints = {
            { mapID = 390, x = 0.8320000000000001, y = 0.306, step = 1, label = "Lorewalker Fu - brewing scenarios" },
            { mapID = 379, x = 0.7140000000000001, y = 0.922, step = 5, label = "The Metal Paw - replacement earned keg" },
        },
        sources = {
            "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=7385#comments:id=1867772",
            "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=7385#comments:id=2331756",
            "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=7385#comments:id=2140242",
        },
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=7385",
        sourceURL = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=7385#comments",
        reviewedAt = "2026-11-13",
    },
    [7386] = {
        achievementId = 7386,
        name = "Grand Expedition Yak",
        source = "Grand Expedition Yak",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        difficulty = "easy",
        difficultyReason = "A direct vendor purchase with a large gold price.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Easy - A direct vendor purchase with a large gold price.\n\n1. Bring 120,000 gold and travel to Uncle Bigpocket at the Grummle Bazaar in Kun-Lai Summit 65.4,61.6. No quest chain or guild membership is required.\n\n2. Buy the GRAND EXPEDITION Yak teaching item, not the much cheaper grey or blonde riding yak, and use it to learn the mount. Check the item name and vendor price before confirming the purchase.\n\n3. Verify the achievement and mount collection. The historical 108,000-gold guild-perk price is obsolete. The utility passengers now include a transmogrifier and repair/vendor service; the original reforging service was removed.",
        stepCount = 3,
        waypoints = { { mapID = 379, x = 0.654, y = 0.616, step = 1, label = "Uncle Bigpocket - Grand Expedition Yak" } },
        sources = {
            "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=7386#comments:id=1812680",
            "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=7386#comments:id=1764102",
        },
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=7386",
        sourceURL = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=7386#comments",
        reviewedAt = "2026-11-13",
    },
    [7437] = {
        achievementId = 7437,
        name = "A Worthy Opponent",
        source = "A Worthy Opponent",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        difficulty = "easy",
        difficultyReason = "Legacy rare kills are simple at high level, but finding every spawn takes travel and waiting.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Easy - Legacy rare kills are simple at high level, but finding every spawn takes travel and waiting.\n\n1. Defeat any ONE of the original Pandaria champions below. A high-level character can handle these legacy rares; a rare drop from the kill is unnecessary.\n\n2. Search this map's champion route: Mister Ferocious (Hozen); Aethis (Jinyu); Krax'ik (Mantid); Kor'nas Nightsavage (Mogu Sorcerer); Morgrinn Crackfang (Mogu Warrior); Urobi the Walker (Pandaren); Sarnak (Saurok); Ferdinand (Yaungol). Visit the marked spawn areas and search nearby patrols/caves. An empty pin means the rare may be dead, patrolling or at another nearby spawn; return later.\n\n3. Search this map's champion route: Bonobos (Hozen); Sele'na (Jinyu); Nal'lak the Ripper (Mantid); Sulik'shor (Mogu Sorcerer); Jonn-Dar (Mogu Warrior); Nasra Spothide (Pandaren); Salyin Warscout (Saurok); Blackhoof (Yaungol). Visit the marked spawn areas and search nearby patrols/caves. An empty pin means the rare may be dead, patrolling or at another nearby spawn; return later.\n\n4. Search this map's champion route: Spriggin (Hozen); Cournith Waterstrider (Jinyu); Torik-Ethis (Mantid); Gaarn the Toxic (Mogu Sorcerer); Qu'nas (Mogu Warrior); Ruun Ghostpaw (Pandaren); Arness the Scale (Saurok); Go-Kan (Yaungol). Visit the marked spawn areas and search nearby patrols/caves. Ruun is upstairs in the Red Crane temple, Cournith inside Fallsong's building and Spriggin atop the southern island's boat platform.\n\n5. Search this map's champion route: Scritch (Hozen); Zai the Outcast (Jinyu); Ski'thik (Mantid); Borginn Darkfist (Mogu Sorcerer); Havak (Mogu Warrior); Ahone the Wanderer (Pandaren); Nessos the Oracle (Saurok); Korda Torros (Yaungol). Visit the marked spawn areas and search nearby patrols/caves. An empty pin means the rare may be dead, patrolling or at another nearby spawn; return later.\n\n6. Search this map's champion route: The Yowler (Hozen); Eshelon (Jinyu); Lith'ik the Stalker (Mantid); Norlaxx (Mogu Sorcerer); Kah'tir (Mogu Warrior); Yul Wildpaw (Pandaren); Siltriss the Sharpener (Saurok); Lon the Bull (Yaungol). Visit the marked spawn areas and search nearby patrols/caves. An empty pin means the rare may be dead, patrolling or at another nearby spawn; return later.\n\n7. Search this map's champion route: Ik-Ik the Nimble (Hozen); Nalash Verdantis (Jinyu); Gar'lok (Mantid); Karr the Darkener (Mogu Sorcerer); Krol the Blade (Mogu Warrior); Ai-Li Skymirror (Pandaren); Omnis Grinlok (Saurok); Dak the Breaker (Yaungol). Visit the marked spawn areas and search nearby patrols/caves. Ik-Ik is underground at Kypari Zar; search Gar'lok's possible houses near Heart of Fear and Omnis's Briny Muck patrol.\n\n8. Search this map's champion route: Major Nanners (Hozen); Sahn Tidehunter (Jinyu); Kal'tik the Blight (Mantid); Kang the Soul Thief (Mogu Sorcerer); Urgolax (Mogu Warrior); Ai-Ran the Shifting Cloud (Pandaren); Moldo One-Eye (Saurok); Yorik Sharpeye (Yaungol). Visit the marked spawn areas and search nearby patrols/caves. Use Zidormi's earlier Vale, not the Black Empire assault versions of similarly named enemies.\n\n9. Tag each needed champion with your own attack and confirm its kill credit. Interrupt Pandaren heals, avoid Jinyu water attacks and do not stand in Mogu ground effects on a low-level character. Revisit only unchecked names/types; buying their toy drops does not count as a champion kill.",
        stepCount = 9,
        waypoints = {
            { mapID = 371, x = 0.426, y = 0.38799999999999996, step = 2, label = "Mister Ferocious - Hozen search area" },
            { mapID = 371, x = 0.366, y = 0.508, step = 2, label = "Aethis - Jinyu search area" },
            { mapID = 371, x = 0.396, y = 0.626, step = 2, label = "Krax'ik - Mantid search area" },
            {
                mapID = 371,
                x = 0.43799999999999994,
                y = 0.7240000000000001,
                step = 2,
                label = "Kor'nas Nightsavage - Mogu Sorcerer search area",
            },
            { mapID = 371, x = 0.408, y = 0.152, step = 2, label = "Morgrinn Crackfang - Mogu Warrior search area" },
            { mapID = 371, x = 0.574, y = 0.7140000000000001, step = 2, label = "Urobi the Walker - Pandaren search area" },
            { mapID = 371, x = 0.6459999999999999, y = 0.742, step = 2, label = "Sarnak - Saurok search area" },
            { mapID = 371, x = 0.542, y = 0.424, step = 2, label = "Ferdinand - Yaungol search area" },
            { mapID = 376, x = 0.156, y = 0.322, step = 3, label = "Bonobos - Hozen search area" },
            { mapID = 376, x = 0.528, y = 0.28600000000000003, step = 3, label = "Sele'na - Jinyu search area" },
            {
                mapID = 376,
