    [7438] = {
        achievementId = 7438,
        name = "Could We Find More Like That?",
        source = "Could We Find More Like That?",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        difficulty = "easy",
        difficultyReason = "Legacy rare kills are simple at high level, but finding every spawn takes travel and waiting.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Easy - Legacy rare kills are simple at high level, but finding every spawn takes travel and waiting.\n\n1. Defeat at least one champion of EACH of eight types: Hozen, Jinyu, Mantid, Mogu Sorcerer, Mogu Warrior, Pandaren, Saurok and Yaungol. Eight arbitrary rares can fail if they repeat a type; use the labels below.\n\n2. Search this map's champion route: Mister Ferocious (Hozen); Aethis (Jinyu); Krax'ik (Mantid); Kor'nas Nightsavage (Mogu Sorcerer); Morgrinn Crackfang (Mogu Warrior); Urobi the Walker (Pandaren); Sarnak (Saurok); Ferdinand (Yaungol). Visit the marked spawn areas and search nearby patrols/caves. An empty pin means the rare may be dead, patrolling or at another nearby spawn; return later.\n\n3. Search this map's champion route: Bonobos (Hozen); Sele'na (Jinyu); Nal'lak the Ripper (Mantid); Sulik'shor (Mogu Sorcerer); Jonn-Dar (Mogu Warrior); Nasra Spothide (Pandaren); Salyin Warscout (Saurok); Blackhoof (Yaungol). Visit the marked spawn areas and search nearby patrols/caves. An empty pin means the rare may be dead, patrolling or at another nearby spawn; return later.\n\n4. Search this map's champion route: Spriggin (Hozen); Cournith Waterstrider (Jinyu); Torik-Ethis (Mantid); Gaarn the Toxic (Mogu Sorcerer); Qu'nas (Mogu Warrior); Ruun Ghostpaw (Pandaren); Arness the Scale (Saurok); Go-Kan (Yaungol). Visit the marked spawn areas and search nearby patrols/caves. Ruun is upstairs in the Red Crane temple, Cournith inside Fallsong's building and Spriggin atop the southern island's boat platform.\n\n5. Search this map's champion route: Scritch (Hozen); Zai the Outcast (Jinyu); Ski'thik (Mantid); Borginn Darkfist (Mogu Sorcerer); Havak (Mogu Warrior); Ahone the Wanderer (Pandaren); Nessos the Oracle (Saurok); Korda Torros (Yaungol). Visit the marked spawn areas and search nearby patrols/caves. An empty pin means the rare may be dead, patrolling or at another nearby spawn; return later.\n\n6. Search this map's champion route: The Yowler (Hozen); Eshelon (Jinyu); Lith'ik the Stalker (Mantid); Norlaxx (Mogu Sorcerer); Kah'tir (Mogu Warrior); Yul Wildpaw (Pandaren); Siltriss the Sharpener (Saurok); Lon the Bull (Yaungol). Visit the marked spawn areas and search nearby patrols/caves. An empty pin means the rare may be dead, patrolling or at another nearby spawn; return later.\n\n7. Search this map's champion route: Ik-Ik the Nimble (Hozen); Nalash Verdantis (Jinyu); Gar'lok (Mantid); Karr the Darkener (Mogu Sorcerer); Krol the Blade (Mogu Warrior); Ai-Li Skymirror (Pandaren); Omnis Grinlok (Saurok); Dak the Breaker (Yaungol). Visit the marked spawn areas and search nearby patrols/caves. Ik-Ik is underground at Kypari Zar; search Gar'lok's possible houses near Heart of Fear and Omnis's Briny Muck patrol.\n\n8. Search this map's champion route: Major Nanners (Hozen); Sahn Tidehunter (Jinyu); Kal'tik the Blight (Mantid); Kang the Soul Thief (Mogu Sorcerer); Urgolax (Mogu Warrior); Ai-Ran the Shifting Cloud (Pandaren); Moldo One-Eye (Saurok); Yorik Sharpeye (Yaungol). Visit the marked spawn areas and search nearby patrols/caves. Use Zidormi's earlier Vale, not the Black Empire assault versions of similarly named enemies.\n\n9. Tag each needed champion with your own attack and confirm its kill credit. Interrupt Pandaren heals, avoid Jinyu water attacks and do not stand in Mogu ground effects on a low-level character. Revisit only unchecked names/types; buying their toy drops does not count as a champion kill.",
